      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Awesome!  I can write up some bring-up instructions if that would be helpful to anyone.  I haven't tried bringing it up on a breadboard using the breadboard breakout but it should be possible.\nOr the \"v0\" version of the host board is pretty cheap to get JLC to make (useful if you already have a Tiny Tapeout QSPI PMOD): https://codeberg.org/rebelmike/ws01-tinyQV-mobo-alpha/src/branch/v0\nOr in a couple of weeks time I should have been able to verify the more fully featured one pictured above, which will obviously be a bit more expensive but should run standalone (though you'll still need a Pico or something to program it plus a UART adapter).",
      "author": {
